# 21. Review/repair process

Use at most two review rounds.

## Round 1

Main agent produces a complete compiled Common implementation.

Then all four subagents review independently.

Main agent:

1. verifies every finding;
2. deduplicates findings;
3. classifies them as blocking / should-fix / optional;
4. repairs all accepted blocking and should-fix issues;
5. rebuilds.

## Round 2

Subagents review only the repaired result and regression risks.

Main agent performs final repairs, full build, audits, and freeze.

Stop after Round 2.

Do not endlessly polish.

